{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1610","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1610","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1610\",\"parent_revision\":\"33f309404f5a3c3ac9f143473f1ea4088e52a920782968dc0c6fc66fac7f3ace\",\"root_revision\":\"33f309404f5a3c3ac9f143473f1ea4088e52a920782968dc0c6fc66fac7f3ace\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`test_backlog_core_operations.py` and `test_batch_section_writes.py` create real GitHub issues during test runs when the GitHub mock is absent or incomplete. Evidence: 30+ issues with titles \\\"Desc Item\\\", \\\"No Issue Item\\\", \\\"Old Title\\\" were found open in the tracker and closed as `not_planned` on 2026-04-06.\\n\\nRoot cause (design): The tests call operations that reach the GitHub backend. Some tests patch `try_get_github` to return `None`, but tests that create items via `backlog_add` do not consistently mock the full GitHub integration path. When `GITHUB_TOKEN` is set in the test environment, real API calls succeed and real issues are created.\\n\\nThe design issue is not individual missing mocks \u2014 it is that the test suite has no enforced isolation boundary. Tests can reach live GitHub silently.\\n\\nFix design:\\n1. Set `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory` in the pytest fixture or `conftest.py` for all tests in `test_backlog_core_operations.py` and `test_batch_section_writes.py`\\n2. Verify that the memory backend satisfies all operations these tests exercise\\n3. Add a CI assertion that no GitHub issues are created during `pytest` runs (verify issue count before/after, or assert no `GITHUB_TOKEN` calls occur)\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/` creates zero GitHub issues when run against a repo with an active `GITHUB_TOKEN`\\n- [ ] `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory` is set in the test environment via `conftest.py` or equivalent for all backlog operation tests\\n- [ ] The memory backend returns correct results for all operations tested in `test_backlog_core_operations.py` and `test_batch_section_writes.py`\\n- [ ] CI workflow verifies no live GitHub calls occur during unit test phase\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **ensure backlog_core tests are fully isolated from live GitHub** so that **running tests does not pollute the real issue tracker with test artifacts**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed during session 2026-04-06 \u2014 30 test artifact issues found in tracker\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-06\\n- **Evidence**: Issues #1551\u20131592, #1483\u20131490 all with \\\"not_planned\\\" closure\\n- **In-flight**: PR #1613 (branch: fix/test-isolation-and-hook-format) claims to fix this via `_block_github_io(autouse=True)` fixture\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Grooming\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### RT-ICA Snapshot (2026-04-07)\\n\\n**Goal:** Enforce test isolation so no test can reach the live GitHub backend without explicitly opting in.\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Evidence |\\n|-----------|--------|----------|\\n| Root cause identified | AVAILABLE | Backend singleton cached at module level; per-test mocking too late; no autouse fixture |\\n| `reset_config()` exists | AVAILABLE | `backlog_core/backend_protocol.py:907\u2013914` |\\n| `InMemoryBackend` fully implemented | AVAILABLE | `backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py` |\\n| PR #1613 in-flight | AVAILABLE | PR #1613 open, adds `_block_github_io(autouse=True)` to `conftest.py` |\\n| PR #1613 covers both test files | AVAILABLE | PR #1613 modifies `tests/conftest.py`, `test_backlog_core_operations.py`, `test_batch_section_writes.py` |\\n| CI assertion included in PR #1613 | MISSING | PR #1613 test plan does not mention CI assertion (AC 4) |\\n\\n**Decision: APPROVED** \u2014 fix is clear and PR #1613 provides near-complete coverage.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type:** Defect \u2014 no enforced isolation boundary (design flaw)\\n\\n**5-Whys:**\\n1. Why did 30+ real issues get created? \u2192 Tests reached live GitHub when `GITHUB_TOKEN` was set\\n2. Why did tests reach live GitHub? \u2192 No autouse fixture blocked GitHub I/O\\n3. Why was there no autouse fixture? \u2192 Only per-test mocking existed; backend singleton not reset\\n4. Why wasn't singleton reset? \u2192 `reset_config()` exists but was not called between tests\\n5. **Root fix:** `_block_github_io(autouse=True)` fixture in `conftest.py` that sets `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory` and calls `reset_config()`\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Role | Change |\\n|------|------|--------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` | **Fix target** | Add `_block_github_io(autouse=True)` fixture (PR #1613) |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` | Affected test file | Covered by PR #1613 |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_batch_section_writes.py` | Affected test file | Covered by PR #1613 |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` | `reset_config()` | No change; function already exists at line 907 |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py` | Isolation mechanism | No change; already implemented |\\n| CI workflow (`.github/workflows/`) | AC 4 gap | CI assertion for no live GitHub calls NOT yet in PR #1613 |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` (primary fix)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` (reset_config, line ~907)\\n\\n### In-Flight: PR #1613\\n\\nPR #1613 (branch: `fix/test-isolation-and-hook-format`) addresses this issue. Modified files include `tests/conftest.py`, `test_backlog_core_operations.py`, `test_batch_section_writes.py`.\\n\\n**Gap**: CI assertion (AC 4 \u2014 verify no live GitHub calls during unit test phase) is NOT included in PR #1613.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Small (S)** \u2014 PR #1613 covers the main fix. Remaining work:\\n- Verify PR #1613 against all 4 ACs before merge\\n- Add CI assertion for AC 4 (either in PR #1613 or as a follow-up)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"502e0f8eb04982698e3a1c3b8d1e2164f55e7d61886ba8997c781de977f9e4f8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCv3Eg\"}"}